# SYNOPSIS

```usage
mkdir [-p] [-m mode] dir...
```

# DESCRIPTION

`mkdir` makes each directory <dir>.
A <dir> that exists already is an error.

: `-p`
  Make each missing directory on the way to <dir> first, and say nothing of one that exists.
: `-m`
  The directory's mode, in octal, at most `777`.

# SEE ALSO

rm(1), ls(1)

# DIAGNOSTICS

The exit string is `error` if a <dir> couldn't be made, each one reported, such as `mkdir: box already exists`.

# BUGS

Directories have no modes: `-m`'s <mode> is checked and not kept.
